From aca6fe58d7abc521dc2c57aaceffa6deb8f88fa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TalentOS Contributor <contributor@example.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:57:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: add local development setup guide and backend bootstrap

- Add docker-compose.yml services for Postgres, Redis, and Qdrant
- Add minimal FastAPI backend entrypoint (backend/main.py) with a
  /health endpoint so the setup can be verified end-to-end
- Add pyproject.toml with backend dependencies
- Add .env.example documenting required environment variables
- Add docs/setup.md: step-by-step local dev setup guide
- Update .gitignore for Python artifacts and .env

Currently backend/main.py, docker-compose.yml, and pyproject.toml were
empty placeholders, so there was no way for a new contributor to
actually run the project locally. This fills that gap with a minimal,
verified-working setup (tested: docker-compose.yml validates as YAML,
pyproject.toml validates as TOML, and the FastAPI app boots and returns
200 on / and /health).

Closes: good-first-issue (local dev setup / docs)
