@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+# Local Development Setup
+
+This guide walks you through running TalentOS locally: the datastores
+(PostgreSQL, Redis, Qdrant) and the backend API (FastAPI).
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+Make sure you have the following installed:
+
+* [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/) and Docker Compose
+* [Python 3.11+](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
+* [Git](https://git-scm.com/)
+
+## 1. Clone the repository
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/Bugbaar/TalentOS.git
+cd TalentOS
+```
+
+## 2. Configure environment variables
+
+Copy the example env file and adjust values if needed (the defaults work
+out of the box with the Docker Compose setup below):
+
+```bash
+cp .env.example .env
+```
+
+## 3. Start the datastores
+
+TalentOS depends on three services in local development: PostgreSQL,
+Redis, and Qdrant. Start them with Docker Compose:
+
+```bash
+docker compose up -d
+```
+
+Check that all three containers are healthy:
+
+```bash
+docker compose ps
+```
+
+You should see `talentos_postgres`, `talentos_redis`, and
+`talentos_qdrant` running.
+
+To stop the services later:
+
+```bash
+docker compose down
+```
+
+## 4. Set up the backend
+
+Create a virtual environment and install dependencies:
+
+```bash
+cd backend
+python -m venv .venv
+source .venv/bin/activate   # On Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
+pip install -e ".[dev]"     # installs from pyproject.toml
+```
+
+## 5. Run the backend API
+
+```bash
+uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
+```
+
+The API will be available at `http://localhost:8000`. You can verify
+everything is wired up correctly by hitting the health check endpoint:
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:8000/health
+```
+
+A healthy response looks like:
+
+```json
+{
+  "status": "healthy",
+  "database_url_configured": true,
+  "redis_url_configured": true,
+  "qdrant_url_configured": true
+}
+```
+
+## 6. Frontend (Next.js)
+
+The frontend package has not been scaffolded yet. Once
+`frontend/` is added, this section will be updated with the equivalent
+`npm install` / `npm run dev` steps.
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+| Problem | Likely cause |
+|---|---|
+| `docker compose up` fails to bind a port | Another local service is already using 5432, 6379, or 6333 — stop it or change the port mapping in `docker-compose.yml`. |
+| `/health` shows a config value as `false` | Your `.env` wasn't loaded — confirm you copied `.env.example` to `.env` and that you're running `uvicorn` from a shell where it's picked up (or that you export the vars). |
+| `pip install -e ".[dev]"` fails | Confirm you're on Python 3.11+ (`python --version`) and that your virtual environment is activated. |
+
+## Next steps
+
+Once your environment is running, check the `good-first-issue` and
+`help-wanted` labels on GitHub Issues for a place to start contributing.
+See [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md) for the PR workflow.
